1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Research on Chen Fengtai's lineage: Guangdong Nanxiong lineage (from Chen Wen to Chen You) http://bbs.chens.org.cn/fengtai/show.aspx?id=444&cid=13
2 CONT
2 CONT The fifth ancestor of Guangdong: Chen Xuan, also known as Chen You, is the second son of "Chen Fengtai". He had three sons: Longge, Fengge, and Linge (also known as: Longhe, Fenghe, and Linhe). In the past, it was said that Chen Y
2 CONC ou moved from Zhuji Lane, Nanxiong, Guangdong to Shitou Township, Gugangzhou, in the first year of Kaixi in the Southern Song Dynasty (i.e. 1205), and was regarded as the great ancestor of the six villages of the Taishan Chen fami
2 CONC ly, according to the "Chen Xinhui Shitou Genealogy". (However, according to the "Chazhou" genealogy of Liucun, Chen You, as the ancestor, moved south after "passing the Mingjing exam", and the year was not mentioned. According to 
2 CONC Chen Ren's "Yizhi", "At that time, there were seven brothers, 28 sons and nephews, and more than 30 clan brothers. Some came with them, some secretly stayed in their hometown, some returned to the alley to sell their property and 
2 CONC missed their hometown and returned to Fujian, and some left." The seven sons fled and scattered, which should be one year after Chen Fengtai and Kuang Yuping "submitted a memorial to slow down the Jin attack on the Yuan Dynasty", 
2 CONC that is, the tenth year of Jiading in the Southern Song Dynasty (i.e. 1217). At that time, the seven sons acted together and agreed to "stop and live by water when encountering conflicts." This date is more credible.
2 CONT
2 CONT Xinhui Shitou Genealogy of Xuanzu (from Chen You to Chen Congshan) http://bbs.chens.org.cn/fengtai/show.aspx?id=445&cid=13
2 CONT
2 CONT Chen You is Chen Xuan, the second son of Chen Fengtai. It is said that there is no record in the "Shitou Genealogy" and it was recognized by Chen Yufu. Chen Congshan is also known as Chen Tianxiang, which was also recognized later
2 CONC . He was the founder of the clan in Langmei, Chikan, and is now honored as the "Six Village Ancestor" of the Chen family in Taishan.
2 CONT
2 CONT ☆ The following table 9: From Chen Xuan to Chen Congshan (also known as the Xinhui "Shitou" Genealogy):
2 CONT
2 CONT (A total of 5 generations, directly extending to the 83rd-87th ancestors)
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the beginning of my family's ancestral records of all male names from generation to generation. This section is also called the "Shitou" genealogy because we lived in Shitou, Xinhui. As mentioned above As explained in the 
2 CONC first table, the old genealogy only recorded the name of the ancestor Chen You. The middle three generations were supplemented by Chen Yufu during the reign of Emperor Kangxi of the Qing Dynasty. Because before him, only Chen Tian
2 CONC xiang, also known as Chen Congshan, was the ancestor of Langmei. Currently, the Chen Clan Clan Network has a detailed introduction.
2 CONT
2 CONT Table 9: Ancestor, key person
2 CONT
2 CONT Chen Xuan (i.e. Chen You)
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers:
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants:
2 CONT
2 CONT Related historical materials and comments/
2 CONT
2 CONT Direct lineage extended to the 83rd generation ancestor
2 CONT
2 CONT The first generation ancestor after Nanxiong: Chen Xuan, also known as Chen You, is the second son of "Chen Fengtai". He had three sons: Longge, Fengge, and Linge (also known as: Longhe, Fenghe, and Linhe). Chen You moved from Zhu
2 CONC ji Lane, Nanxiong, Guangdong to Shitou Township, Gugangzhou, in the first year of Kaixi in the Southern Song Dynasty (i.e. 1205), and was regarded as the great ancestor of the Taishan Chen family. This is recorded in the "Chen Xin
2 CONC hui Shitou Genealogy".
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.chens.org.cn/show.aspx?id=30&cid=13
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of Xinhui Chen Clan Xuanzu [%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%9F%EF%BC%9A2006-08-28] Source: Xinhui Chen Clan Genealogy Author: Anonymous
2 CONT
2 CONT Chen Hui's second son Xuan, whose taboo name is You, whose alias is Nanqiao, whose courtesy name is Shidao, was born in the seventh year of Chunxi in the Southern Song Dynasty (1180 AD). He was a tribute student in the Song Dynast
2 CONC y. He founded Xiadong in Xinhui (now Xiadong, Yayao Town, Heshan City), and later moved to Shixi Village (now Shitou, Tangxia, Xinhui). His wife was He, and he had three sons: Longge, Fengge, and Linge
2 CONT
2 CONT Taizu Xuan's eldest son Longge, whose taboo name is Dao, whose courtesy name is Mengxiao, was a counselor in the Song Dynasty. He was born in the sixth year of Qingyuan (1200 AD) and lived separately in Zhishan Lane, Chaolian Town
2 CONC ship, Xinhui.
2 CONT The second son Fengge, whose taboo name was Kao (Qiao), whose courtesy name was Zhongyi and whose pseudonym was Jingyi, was born on September 26, the second year of Chunyou in the Southern Song Dynasty (1242 AD) and died in the se
2 CONC cond year of Hongwu in the Ming Dynasty (1369 AD) at the age of 128. His wife was Xie and his son was Hui'an. They lived separately in Shitou, Xinhui.
2 CONT The third son Linge, whose courtesy name was Jici, lived separately in Zaodian Village, Chayuan, Dongguan. (Mingli Hall)
2 CONT The second son of Fengge, Hui'an, whose taboo name was Di and whose pseudonym was Mingyan, his wife was Xie and he had four sons: Renfu, Yifu, Lifu, Zhifu
