1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Endnotes from http://www3.fitnyc.edu/gene_chin/tree
2 CONT
2 CONT 應隆 Yëin Lũng (Yīnglóng) was 希堯 Hï Ngẽl's third son. He married a woman from the Yï 余 (Yú) family. He had two sons: 必榮 Bēik Vẽin and 必恩 Bēik Yïn. His tomb was in Hoi Pein 開平 (Kāipíng) in the shape of a dragon facing east. He had an
2 CONC other tomb in Xäm Gâp 三合 (Sānhé) in the shape of a child reciting from a book facing ENE 3/4N or 60 degrees. In mid-spring of [1984] his tomb in Xäm Gâp 三合 (Sānhé) was renovated. 
