1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Endnotes from http://www3.fitnyc.edu/gene_chin/tree
2 CONT
2 CONT 定南 Èin Nãm (Dìngnán) gave his second son, Ruìguī 瑞珪 Xuì Gï, to his third older brother, Ānnán 安南 Ön Nãm, to raise as his own son because Ānnán 安南 Ön Nãm did not have any sons of his own. Dìngnán 定南 Èin Nãm was born in 1441 C.E. He
2 CONC  died on the twelfth day of the twelfth moon in the year 1499 C.E. at the age of 58. His wife from the Zhū 朱Jï clan was buried in Yùhuái 玉槐 Ngùk Vâi. The landscape of the tomb, which faces south, is in the shape of a big seat for 
2 CONC a fairy. His second wife from the Liáng 梁 Lëng family was buried in Huángtián 黃田 Võng Hẽin. The landscape of the tomb, which faces west, is in the shape of a snake. 
